WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
Here is a world map, with the
Equator running across the middle.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.570
This is Nairobi, the capital
of Kenya, in East Africa.

3
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.610
It sits almost on the Equator.

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.130
Shouldn't it be boiling hot?

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.410
Yet Nairobi is warm all year,

6
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.290
on average about eighteen to
twenty-two degrees Celsius.

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.630
So why isn't a city so close
to the Equator boiling hot?

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.610
In this mission, you'll learn
to compare places like a

9
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.770
geographer, using six headings.

10
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.470
You'll sort physical geography
from human geography,

11
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.010
and locate places on a world map.

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.490
And you'll build a profile
of the Nairobi region.

13
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.530
Your mission: explain why Nairobi
is warm, but not boiling hot.
